node 6_20260822-020917 codegen_edits llm_response: Looking at this GEMM kernel, I identified a concrete shared-memory bank-conflict issue in the `As` tile reads: with `BM=128` and 32 banks, the 8 sub-tile rows accessed simultaneously by a warp (`threadRow*TM` for `TM=8`) collapse into only 4 distinct bank groups, causing 2-way bank conflicts on every compute-loop shared memory read of `As`. I fix this by padding each 8-element row-group in the `As` shared memory tile by 4 extra floats (stride 12 instead of 8 per group), which spreads the 8 simultaneous accesses across all 32 banks with no overlap, while keeping the vectorized `float4` reads/writes correct and contiguous within each group.

