node 4_20260822-024022 codegen_edits llm_response: Looking at this matvec kernel, the workload is memory-bandwidth bound (A matrix ~8GB must be read once). The main structural improvement available without changing precision or falling back to libraries is to **pipeline the shared-memory tile loads of B** so that the global-memory load of the next K-tile overlaps with the warp's compute on the current tile, hiding load latency behind FMA work (double-buffered shared memory).

