Reducing `K_TILE` shrinks the double-buffered shared memory footprint substantially (from 64KB to 16KB per block), allowing multiple blocks to be co-resident per SM. This directly improves memory-level parallelism (more outstanding loads in flight), which is critical for bandwidth-bound kernels like this one, without touching the compute/pipelining logic.

