node 8_20260822-053233 codegen_edits llm_response: Looking at this LayerNorm implementation, I can see it's a reduction+elementwise (normalization) kernel. The `reduce_kernel` currently uses `atomicAdd` to accumulate partial sums into `sum_out[n]`/`sqsum_out[n]` from up to 64 blocks per row (`chunk_blocks_y`), causing significant atomic contention on the same memory location across many concurrent blocks. 

I'll eliminate this atomic contention by having each block write its partial sum to a unique slot in an expanded buffer (size `N * chunk_blocks_y`), then have `finalize_kernel` perform a cheap serial sum over the small `chunk_blocks_y` dimension per row instead of relying on atomics. This removes serialization from concurrent atomic writes while preserving identical numerical results.

