node 2_20260822-071323 codegen_edits llm_response: Looking at this convolution kernel, I can see it already implements CTA-level spatial tiling with shared-memory staging of the input tile. However, each thread block only computes outputs for a **single output channel**, meaning the same input tile (loaded into shared memory) is redundantly reloaded from global memory for every output channel. 

I'll implement **register blocking across output channels**: process multiple output channels per thread block, reusing the same shared-memory input tile across all of them. Each thread accumulates results for several output channels simultaneously, reading each shared-memory input value once and reusing it across multiple weight multiplications — reducing shared-memory traffic and amortizing the input tile load across more useful compute.

