Since the kernel is already cooperative and tiled, I'll apply optimization **#4: add register blocking** — specifically, extending the register blocking from only the width dimension (WPT) to also cover the height dimension (HPT). This increases weight-value reuse (each fetched weight value from shared memory is now reused across both height and width sub-tiles per thread) and reduces the number of threads needed per block while increasing work per thread, improving arithmetic intensity and reducing shared-memory traffic overhead relative to compute.

