**Key inefficiency found:** In the inner compute loop, the loop order is `oc -> ry -> rx -> ky -> kx`, which means the same input pixel value from shared memory (`smem_row[kx*dilation]`) gets re-read from shared memory **OC_TILE (16) times** — once per output channel iteration — even though it doesn't depend on `oc` at all.

**Optimization applied:** Reorder loops to `ry -> rx -> ky -> kx -> oc`, so each input value is loaded from shared memory **once** into a register and reused across all 16 output channels in the inner-most loop. This is a shared-memory reuse / register-blocking optimization that significantly cuts redundant shared-memory traffic without changing any convolution semantics.

