node 4_20260822-082221 codegen_edits llm_response: Looking at this convolution kernel, it's already a cooperative tiled implementation (shared memory staging for weights and input, register blocking with OW_COARSEN). However, weights are re-staged into shared memory for *every* block even though many blocks share the same `(batch, out_channel)` pair but differ only in spatial `(od, oh)` position — this causes massive redundant shared-memory loading work across the huge grid (D_out*H_out ≈ 648 blocks per (batch,oc) pair). I apply **improved spatial tiling**: have each block process multiple `(od, oh)` positions in a loop, amortizing the weight staging cost (and per-block launch overhead) over `OD_OH_TILE` spatial locations instead of just one.

