**Chosen optimization: Register blocking** — Each thread currently computes only 1 output pixel per output-channel-tile iteration. I'll have each thread compute `OW_PER_THREAD=2` adjacent output pixels along the width dimension, reusing the same shared-memory weight value (`wrow[kw]`) and loop overhead across multiple outputs. This increases arithmetic intensity per shared-memory load/thread, reduces the redundant weight-fetch overhead relative to FMA count, and halves the number of threads needed per output tile (improving occupancy per SM due to fewer resident threads for the same work).

