node 7_20260822-111604 codegen_edits llm_response: Looking at this kernel, I identify it as a GEMM-like fused attention kernel (QK^T and softmax@V matmuls with shared memory staging). 

**Structural weakness found:** In the output computation phase (`softmax(scores) @ V`), the loop `for (int d8 = threadIdx.x; d8 < dim8; d8 += blockDim.x)` only utilizes `dim8` threads (128, since dim=1024, dim8=dim>>3=128), but `blockDim.x` = THREADS = 256. This means **half the threads sit idle** during this hot loop (which iterates over the full seqlen=256 with BLOCK_M=16 FMA operations per iteration) — a clear occupancy/utilization red flag causing wasted compute cycles.

**Optimization applied:** Redistribute work across all threads by partitioning the BLOCK_M query rows across groups of threads (each group owns one `d8` index), so that all 256 threads perform useful work instead of half being idle.

